@startuml voiceover-state-machine
title Voice-over track lifecycle (UI + asset)

skinparam shadowing false

[*] --> Hidden

Hidden : track not mounted
Hidden : (flag off OR draft not reel/story)
Hidden --> Empty : flag on && video-capable draft

state Empty {
  Empty : no voiceover asset
  Empty : script editable (pre-filled from narration)
  Empty : voice selectable
}

Empty --> Generating : click "Générer"\n[draftId present]
Empty --> Empty : edit script / pick voice

state Generating {
  Generating : POST in flight
  Generating : controls disabled, estimator bar
}

Generating --> Ready : 200 { media }\n(asset created, role='voiceover')
Generating --> Error : 4xx/5xx\n(409 no-key, 502 upstream, 400, 429)

state Ready {
  Ready : asset playable (AudioTrackPlayer)
  Ready : "Régénérer" available
}

Ready --> Stale : edit script / change voice\n(asset still valid)
Ready --> Generating : click "Régénérer"
Stale --> Generating : click "Régénérer" (emphasized)
Stale --> Ready : revert edits to match asset

Error --> Generating : click "Réessayer"
Error --> Empty : (no asset was written)\nedit & retry

note right of Generating
  mock  : ffmpeg anullsrc, NO network, cost 0
  live+key : real TTS via reused node core
  live+no-key : never enters Generating success;
                routes straight to Error (409)
end note

note bottom of Ready
  Ready asset participates in:
   - Compose (../02_compose) reads role='voiceover'
   - Publish confirm track summary (D4)
end note

Ready --> [*] : draft published / discarded
@enduml
